  "body": "PR #3798 adds provider setup controls. It does not add the live provider tests requested on #3781.\nThe latest review identifies this missing work.\n\nThe maintainer requested: \"setup the various different providers api keys and do some automated tests before a user (me) gets involved\".\nSource: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3781\n\nAdd ignored tests in the `live-ai` lane for Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, and Ollama.\nUse the cheapest suitable model for each provider.\nRun a cloud test only when its provider key is in the process environment.\nRun the Ollama test only when the local server answers.\nWithout credentials or a local server, print a clear skip message and pass.\nNever print a key in test output or logs.\n\nCheck these steps for each provider:\n- Look up the key from the environment, then the OS keychain.\n- Confirm that the status reaches Ready.\n- Send one short chat turn and confirm returned text.\n- Call `get_job` on a small fixture project and confirm success.\n- Use a wrong key and confirm the key rejected status.\n\nThe maintainer runner supplies keys only through the test environment.\nRun this lane before the reporter hand-test for #3781.\nThe same lane supports #3782 and #3783.\n\nDone means: the ignored lane covers each step and documents a run before the reporter hand-test.\n\neffort:high - The tests span provider transport, UI readiness, and fixture tool calls.\n\nRefs #3781. Found in the review of #3798.\n",
